keys:

    ctrl+t (or ctrl+n)      new shell tab
    ctrl+w                  close tab
    ctrl+→/← (or ctrl+f/b)  next / previous tab


install to `~/.local/bin/tabs`:

    curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sueszli/tmux-tabs/master/install.sh | bash


update with:

    curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sueszli/tmux-tabs/master/update.sh | bash


make sure `~/.local/bin` is on your path, then run `tabs`.
to use `tabs` when you type `tmux`, add `alias tmux=tabs` to your shell config.
`command tmux` still runs the real tmux.


development:

    make deps       # fetch pinned Bats-core, bats-support and bats-assert
    make test       # run the Bash test suite; requires jq
    make fmt        # format Bash and Bats files; requires shfmt
    make lint       # syntax, ShellCheck and formatting checks
    make check      # lint + tests, without modifying files
    make precommit  # format, then run all checks

Bats and its assertion helpers live in .tools/ (gitignored). No sudo or
runtime dependency is added. make deps requires git and network access;
subsequent test runs work offline. Install ShellCheck and shfmt with your
package manager (for example, brew install shellcheck shfmt on macOS).

Tests live in tests/*.bats. Shared setup in tests/test_helper.bash loads
bats-assert, sources tmux-tabs.sh, and creates a temporary HOME for each
test. tests/tmux-stub.sh records tmux calls instead of touching real sessions.
All test scripts, including tests/bootstrap.sh, live directly in tests/.
Use `run command`, `assert_success`, `assert_failure`, and `assert_output`
to test behavior. Bats runs commands under `run` in a subshell: inspect
files or captured output rather than expecting variable changes to persist.

To run a subset:

    .tools/bats-core/bin/bats tests/hooks.bats
    .tools/bats-core/bin/bats --filter 'session start' tests

Keep sourcing tmux-tabs.sh side-effect-free and add regression tests when
changing hooks or status transitions. Helper libraries are development-only;
the installed script remains standalone.
